BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea4Tea - An All Trans &amp\; Nonbinary Comedy Mutual Aid Fundrais
 er!
DTSTART:20261015T200000
DTEND:20261015T200000
UID:83c5a6434c59888b1dd8832bffe0d131@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:A night of EXCLUSIVELY trans and / or nonbinary comedians spil
 ling the tea for mutual aid directly supporting a family in Gaza We need t
 rans community and solidarity more than ever\, and that&#x27\;s what this 
 comedy show is all about! Come check out a line of EXCLUSIVELY trans and /
  or nonbinary comedians coming together in solidarity to make you belly la
 ugh. All proceeds from the show will go to the Sondos Project\, supporting
  a family of 13 living in Gaza 🏳️‍🌈🍉 Tea4Tea is all about hav
 ing a blast while gathering in community\, celebrating the amazing comedic
  talent in Toronto\, and getting some hard earned trans and queer joy! Thi
 s is an extra special fundraiser edition that is one small part of taking 
 care of each other in hard times. Doors 7 45 pm\, show 8 pm! Hosted and pr
 oduced by Anna Sebastien (@annasebastiencomedy\, they/them\, Just for Laug
 hs Toronto\, Toronto Fringe Festival\, Fresh Hot Babes All Fem &amp\; Quee
 r Comedy) Full line up announcement coming soon! Advanced tickets are $25 
 but all are welcome regardless of means - DM @annasebastiencomedy on Insta
 gram for Pay What You Can tickets / community pricing. All welcome includi
 ng respectful allies who understand this is a trans inclusive space where 
 we don&#x27\;t assume anyone&#x27\;s pronouns\, gender\, or orientation\, 
 etc. Again\, this show is all about community - if you have any questions 
 or are nervous about coming out\, please reach out to the producer at @ann
 asebastiencomedy on Instagram or email at anna.sebastien.comedy@gmail.com 
 Hope to see you there! 😊 -- About the fundraiser: Sondos and her family
  of 13 need our help for food and supplies while living in Gaza. Sondos an
 d her family are #388 on @paliliberation&#x27\;s verified families list! C
 heck out the Sondos Project here. This campaign was chosen because it supp
 orts a family directly and because the efforts of local drag artists to ac
 tually do something about the ongoing crisis in Gaza are inspiring AF! Aft
 er compensating comedians (we love paying trans artists for their labour!)
 \, all proceeds will be donated. Receipts of the donation will be posted o
 n the producers Instagram for transperancy. Can&#x27\;t make the show but 
 want to support? Love that. Donate here. And be sure to follow the Sondos 
 Project here. About the venue: The show takes place at Tallboys (838 Bloor
  W\, near Ossington subway station) The show takes place in the theatre sp
 ace in the downstairs area of Tallboys. Take a left when you walk in and h
 ead downstairs! The venue unfortunately has a few barriers to access. Ther
 e is a large step to enter the main bar area. The theatre space and washro
 oms are located down a staircase\, with tight corners from the bottom land
 ing to the theatre. There is also a single step from the basement hallway 
 into the venue room. Once inside\, there is no grade change. The venue has
  a communal bathroom with stalls and urinals\, and a woman&#x27\;s washroo
 m with stalls. There is also an unmarked\, single stall\, gender neutral w
 ashroom with a toilet. There is a full kitchen available until 10 pm\, and
  non-alcoholic and alcoholic beverages available until close No purchase i
 s required on top of your ticket (but we love it when you support the venu
 e if ya can!) ‍
LOCATION:Tallboys Craft Beer House\, 838 Bloor Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/tea4tea---an-all-trans-nonbinary-comedy-mu
 tual-aid-fundraiser
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
